1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,121
Two Hands.

2
00:00:01,171 --> 00:00:03,852
Verifiable quality control for handwritten numbers.

3
00:00:03,902 --> 00:00:05,804
OCR reads the number.

4
00:00:05,854 --> 00:00:09,316
Two Hands checks whether the whole form agrees.

5
00:00:09,366 --> 00:00:12,048
Here, the official record typed 480.

6
00:00:12,098 --> 00:00:13,999
The paper says 180.

7
00:00:14,049 --> 00:00:15,950
Gemma read the paper.

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,283
Mexico counts every tally sheet twice:

9
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:23,569
a fast preliminary capture, then the certified count.

10
00:00:23,619 --> 00:00:27,855
On 6.5% of the polling stations not recounted,

11
00:00:27,905 --> 00:00:32,617
the two official records of the same paper disagree.

12
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:37,855
And 19.2% of national forms fail their own row sum,

13
00:00:37,905 --> 00:00:40,236
in the official capture.

14
00:00:40,286 --> 00:00:45,950
A sum says something is wrong; the photo says which field.

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,354
Gemma, on AMD, reads every field twice:

16
00:00:49,404 --> 00:00:52,759
the digits and the amount in words.

17
00:00:52,809 --> 00:00:55,737
A second, independent reader must agree.

18
00:00:55,787 --> 00:00:59,141
The referee is the paper's own arithmetic.

19
00:00:59,191 --> 00:01:01,269
Every check holds: accepted.

20
00:01:01,319 --> 00:01:05,950
One fails: a person sees the field, with its photo.

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,080
Here is a real sheet.

22
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:13,776
Gemma read 23, in digits and in words.

23
00:01:13,826 --> 00:01:18,472
But the rows sum to 366, not 466.

24
00:01:18,522 --> 00:01:24,211
On the site, the same sheet: routed to a person.

25
00:01:24,261 --> 00:01:29,950
The paper says 123, and with it the sum holds.

26
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,807
Every field gets a receipt.

27
00:01:32,857 --> 00:01:36,617
Verified: it proves the record is unchanged.

28
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:39,950
Not that the reading is right.

29
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,236
Now a live read.

30
00:01:42,286 --> 00:01:46,807
One request to Gemma, on the AMD Token Factory.

31
00:01:46,857 --> 00:01:51,379
We cut the wait; the timer stays on screen.

32
00:01:51,429 --> 00:01:53,664
It took 90 seconds.

33
00:01:53,714 --> 00:01:55,950
Every check holds: accepted.

34
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,495
This is the product.

35
00:01:58,545 --> 00:02:03,586
An auditor brings the typed data and the scans.

36
00:02:03,636 --> 00:02:08,168
Here, the sample: 6,000 fields, checked in seconds.

37
00:02:08,218 --> 00:02:10,714
267 disputes, strongest first.

38
00:02:10,764 --> 00:02:16,314
This one: the capture keyed 75; the paper says 175.

39
00:02:16,364 --> 00:02:19,877
One fingerprint seals the whole report.

40
00:02:19,927 --> 00:02:23,950
Change one number, and the check fails.

41
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,450
The proof.

42
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:30,450
Gemma on AMD read 1,270 real handwritten tally sheets.

43
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:34,950
49 capture errors, confirmed by the certified count.

44
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,450
Recall: 27 of 28 capture errors the certified count reveals,

45
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,950
in one state, pre-registered.

46
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,950
A person re-read the AI-judged disputes blind:

47
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,950
0 read differently.

48
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,719
On Baja California Sur's local actas: 91.6% field match.

49
00:02:54,769 --> 00:02:59,912
The Google Document AI reading the state bought

50
00:02:59,962 --> 00:03:03,950
scored 62.84%, on the same metric.

51
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,250
Same 300 forms, same gate.

52
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:14,400
It accepts 1.8x the forms Qwen does, at the same error rate,

53
00:03:14,450 --> 00:03:17,150
4.6x cheaper, 2.8x faster.

54
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,900
A whole state: Colima.

55
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:25,950
Gemma on AMD read all 982 sheets for 14 cents.

56
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,041
Each strong finding becomes a case in Evolus.

57
00:03:30,091 --> 00:03:35,041
The agent runs on Gemma, on AMD, and drafts it.

58
00:03:35,091 --> 00:03:39,132
A script, not the model, scores the evidence.

59
00:03:39,182 --> 00:03:40,950
The auditor decides.

60
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,915
Mexico's preliminary counts:

61
00:03:42,965 --> 00:03:47,336
INE, 32 state institutes, and their outside auditors.

62
00:03:47,386 --> 00:03:53,231
On 6 June 2027, 32 local elections join the federal midterm.

63
00:03:53,281 --> 00:03:56,178
$1 per sheet audited, proposed:

64
00:03:56,228 --> 00:04:03,055
for Morelos, half a percent of what it paid to run its count.

65
00:04:03,105 --> 00:04:08,950
The first step: a paid shadow-mode pilot on one state's count.

66
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,950
Where it breaks.

67
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,950
On fresh forms, the model read 3114;

68
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,450
the paper says 314.

69
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,450
No sum covers that field.

70
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:24,950
Gate version two sent it to a person.

71
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,117
Every number re-derives from public data, with one command.

72
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:30,367
Two Hands.

73
00:04:30,417 --> 00:04:33,283
Verifiable quality control for handwritten numbers.

74
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:34,950
Running on AMD.
